%% Target-state diagrams; sending, negotiation and measured learning are not implemented.
%% DIAGRAM 1: Component architecture. Render diagrams separately.
flowchart TD
    Owner[Owner: goals, offer, budget, authority] --> UI[Control room]
    UI --> Workflow[Durable workflow and task ownership]
    Workflow --> Manager[GTM orchestrator]
    Manager --> Research[Research specialist]
    Manager --> Sales[Sales specialist]
    Sales <--> Research
    Sales <--> Deal[Deal function: optional separate agent]
    Research --> Gateway[Policy and tool gateway]
    Sales --> Gateway
    Deal --> Gateway
    Gateway --> Connectors[CRM, research, outreach, proposals]
    Connectors --> Events[Authoritative outcomes and events]
    Events --> Workflow
    Events --> Memory[Shared records and evidence]
    Memory --> Manager
    Memory --> Evaluator[Independent evaluator]
    Evaluator --> Playbooks[Versioned playbooks]
    Playbooks --> Manager

%% DIAGRAM 2: Discussion and learning cycle.
flowchart TD
    Evidence[New evidence or mature outcomes] --> Proposals[Independent proposals]
    Proposals --> Challenge[Challenge assumptions and alternatives]
    Challenge --> Decision[Orchestrator decision]
    Decision -->|Test a hypothesis| Design[Preregister baseline, metric, allocation, stop rules]
    Decision -->|Outside authority| Owner[Owner decision]
    Decision -->|No useful change| Keep[Retain current playbook]
    Design --> Test[Bounded live experiment]
    Test --> Review[Evaluator reviews mature outcomes]
    Review -->|Supported within scope| Version[Promote version with rollback target]
    Review -->|Worse| Reject[Reject candidate]
    Review -->|Insufficient evidence| Pending[Continue as planned or mark inconclusive]
    Version --> Evidence
    Reject --> Evidence
    Pending --> Evidence

%% DIAGRAM 3: Account lifecycle.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Discovered
    Discovered --> Researched: sourced account brief
    Researched --> Eligible: inclusion and exclusion checks
    Eligible --> Ready: policy, contact, offer and budget valid
    Ready --> Contacted: provider acknowledgment
    Contacted --> Engaged: relevant reply
    Engaged --> Qualified: qualification rubric met
    Qualified --> Proposal: approved offer delivered
    Proposal --> Negotiation: buyer requests revised terms
    Proposal --> Won: authoritative acceptance
    Negotiation --> Won: authoritative acceptance
    Negotiation --> Lost: confirmed loss
    Engaged --> Nurture: future timing
    Nurture --> Ready: eligibility rechecked
    Contacted --> Suppressed: opt-out
    Engaged --> Suppressed: opt-out
    Ready --> Suppressed: eligibility revoked
    Won --> [*]
    Lost --> [*]
    Suppressed --> [*]
    note right of Suppressed
      Suppression is also a global override
      from any active stage. No automatic revival.
    end note

%% DIAGRAM 4: External action sequence.
sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Sales agent
    participant W as Workflow service
    participant G as Policy gateway
    participant P as Provider
    participant D as Durable records
    A->>W: Structured send request with state version
    W->>D: Acquire account lease and inspect current state
    W->>G: Validate permissions, suppression, terms and budget
    G-->>W: Allow or reject with policy version
    alt Allowed and current
        W->>D: Atomically reserve budget and create outbox action
        W->>P: Send with supported deduplication key
        alt Provider acknowledgment
            P-->>W: Provider message ID
            W->>D: Record success and settle reservation
        else Ambiguous timeout
            W->>D: Record unknown; prohibit blind resend
            W->>P: Reconcile provider state
            W->>D: Record known result or queue exception
        end
    else Rejected or stale
        W->>D: Record rejection and recovery condition
    end
